Hi, I have a question about spatio-temporal models using R-INLA.
Basically, when I fit a model like:

formula = numCases ~ 1 + f(idArea, model = 'bym2', graph = path) +
  f(idArea1, idYear, model = 'iid') + idYear + factor(month)

inla(formula = formula, family = 'poisson',
             data = df_vivax, control.compute = list(cpo = T,
                                                     dic = T, waic = T))

works, and the output it's okay.

But when I use the population too:
formula = numCases ~ 1 + f(idArea, model = 'bym2', graph = path) +
  f(idArea1, idYear, model = 'iid') + idYear + factor(month)  + population

the same poisson specification doesn't work.
I don't know if it is relevant, but the population is the same throughout the years.

Also, the specification that works with poisson doesn't work with zero inflated poisson. Am I missing something?

