the family argument is the distribution of

	y | linear.predictor

and maybe some hyperparameters. the *marginal* of y can be highly skewed
but y|linear predictor can be normal.

like this:

n <- 10000
m <- sqrt(seq(0, 1000, len = n))
y <- rnorm(n, mean = m)
hist(y, prob = TRUE, n = 300)

